          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "El sábado María y su hermana van a casa de su madre. Su madre es profesora y habla español muy bien. Por la mañana comen pan y beben café. Luego María lee un libro y su hermana escribe. Por la tarde caminan hasta la casa de su hermano. Ahora es tarde, pero están bien. Mañana es domingo, y María no trabaja."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Once through, without stopping."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Now answer this before you read it again: how many people are in it?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "culture-pragmatics",
          "title": "Why it's said this way",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four people, and Spanish named each one once. After that they are su madre, su hermana, su hermano — held in place by a single small word you learned a long time ago."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Count what you actually did here. Sixty-one words. Four people. Two days. One page of grammar you already had."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first paragraph in this chapter was forty-seven words and felt like a wall. This one is longer and did not. Nothing was added in between except two more paragraphs — which is the only thing that ever fixes this."
            }
